    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <projectUrl>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/developer/cli/introduction</projectUrl>
    <description>Microsoft PowerPlatform CLI is a simple, single-stop, developer command-line interface (CLI) for developing customizations and extensions for Microsoft PowerPlatform. See project site how to install.</description>
    <summary>This package contains the Microsoft PowerPlatform CLI.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>Please make sure to update your Microsoft Power Platform CLI to the latest version and take advantage of all the latest capabilities by following https://aka.ms/PowerPlatformCLI.
If you are a new user please install the Power Platform CLI directly from here: https://aka.ms/PowerPlatformCLI

2.9.3:
  pages:
    - `pac pages list -v` now reports each site's Data Model Version (Standard / Enhanced) from the Power Pages Sitewide API, reflecting the data model the site is currently running
    - Fixed `pages migrate-datamodel --updateDataModelVersion` reporting a non-recoverable error (System.AggregateException wrapping System.Text.Json.JsonException, "The input does not contain any JSON tokens") when the SetPortalDataModelVersion admin API returns an empty 2xx body, even though the data model version was updated successfully. The empty success response is now handled gracefully instead of crashing.
    - Fixed `pages migrate-datamodel --mode configurationData` (step 1, metadata) marking the migration tracker as Completed even though the migration is not finished until `--mode configurationDataReferences` (step 2, transactional data) also runs. Step 1 now leaves the migration in-progress so the status is accurate and `--updateDataModelVersion` stays gated until step 2 completes; running step 2 after step 1 now resumes the same tracker instead of being blocked or creating a duplicate tracker record.
  admin:
    - New command: `pac admin query` to run Resource Query.
  tool:
    - Moved `init-skills` from `pac copilot init-skills` to `pac tool init-skills`.
  Misc:
    - Updated Microsoft.Identity.Client to 4.85.2
    - Updated Microsoft.PowerPlatform.Dataverse.Client to 1.2.26

2.8:
  Managed Identity:
    - Improved certificate handling for plugin component: certificate evaluation now happens server-side, eliminating certificate type (self/fully signed) detection bug caused by differences in trusted root certs between client and server
    - Added support for PluginPackage component type in managed identity commands
    - Added managed identity version 2 (V2) federated identity credential (FIC) support: V2 uses SHA256-hashed issuer/subject DN segments (i/{hash}/s/{hash}) that are safe for certificates whose CN values would fail ESTS validation on V1 paths (trailing/leading dots, slashes, leading/trailing spaces, non-ASCII characters)
    - Added `--version` argument to `show-fic`, `configure-fic`, and `verify-fic` to inspect or configure a specific FIC version (defaults to the version stored on the managed identity record)
    - New `upgrade-version` verb to upgrade a plugin component's managed identity from V0 to V1 to V2. Supports `--target-version` for direct multi-step upgrades (e.g., V0-&gt;V2 in a single operation, no transient V1 state)
    - Auto-detects plugin certificates with characters incompatible with V1 FIC paths and automatically uses V2 instead: `show-fic` displays the V2 subject + warning, `upgrade-version` upgrades directly to V2 (with `--target-version` override surfaced as a warning if user explicitly chose a lower version)
    - Cross-tenant managed identity FIC configuration: automatically acquires a Graph token for the managed identity's tenant when it differs from the auth profile tenant. If cross-tenant Graph access is unavailable, falls back gracefully to clear manual FIC instructions with the issuer/subject/audience values inline (instead of crashing)
    - New "FIC source" line in command output indicates whether the FIC subject was server-generated, client-generated, or hybrid (cert info from server + path built client-side), making it easy to diagnose configuration issues
    - Fixed tenant ID resolution to handle Guid-typed `tenantid` attribute (previously returned null for cross-tenant managed identities, causing wrong-tenant FIC issuer URLs)
    - `upgrade-version --revert-version` now safely guards against silent runtime breakage: blocks the revert when the certificate has problematic CN values that would fail on a lower FIC version, and auto-configures the lower-version FIC if it was never registered (e.g., after a direct V0-&gt;V2 upgrade)
  canvas:
    - unpack - Experimental layout changes:
      - Fixed bug in Experimental layout when TestCase is created, but no steps added
      - Improved error messages to include msapp entry file name
      - Improved control Rules paths to use name of property in JSON path instead of rule index; makes error messages easier to debug
      - Improved `DynamicProperties` paths to use name of property in JSON path instead of index; makes error messages easier to debug.
      - Improved control `Children` paths to use name of control in JSON path instead of index; makes error messages easier to debug. Still detects changed ordering since it's still significant.
    - pack - Experimental layout changes:
      - Improved YAML parser error messages when duplicate keys detected to include the key name and file location.
  Misc:
    - Updated Microsoft.CrmSdk.SolutionPackagerLib to 9.1.1.215, including SolutionPackager YAML source control format support for packing folders with `solutions/*/solution.yml` manifests.
    - Updated Microsoft.PowerApps.Checker.Client to 1.0.0.42
    - Added solution check output for additional messages returned by the Power Apps Checker service
    - Updated Microsoft.Identity.Client to 4.84.1
    - Updated Microsoft.Graph to 5.105.0

2.7:
  canvas:
    - Enable new SourceCode layout for `unpack` and `pack` commands
      - Both commands support a new optional argument `--layout` which can be set explicitly to either `SourceCode` or `Experimental`
      - Existing script automation will still default to the now legacy `Experimental` layout
    - unpack command
      - default for `--layout` argument is `Experimental` to not break existing automation
    - pack command
      - `--layout` is automatically detected from the contents of the `--sources` folder
      - Added argument `--disable-load-from-yaml` to disable loading yaml source code by Power Apps Studio; only supported for `SourceCode` layout
    - create command is now deprecated as internally it uses the legacy 'Experimental' layout
  copilot:
    - New `quarantine` command to quarantine/unquarantine a bot.
  Misc:
    - Updated Azure.Identity to 1.21.0

